WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.046 --> 00:00:00.879
(crowd cheer)

00:00:00.879 --> 00:00:01.712
- [Crowd Member] Elon, Elon.

00:00:01.712 --> 00:00:05.070
- [Narrator] Elon Musk, at $330 billion,

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:07.950
was the richest man in the world.

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:08.783
But then.

00:00:08.783 --> 00:00:10.410
- [News Reader] Tesla
stock has plummeted more

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:14.370
than 65% since the start of 2022.

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:16.500
- He's no longer the world's richest man

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:18.450
and his EV company is on track

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:22.170
for having its worst year
in the stocks history.

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:24.180
- [Narrator] By the end of 2022,

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:27.600
Musk lost more than half
his net worth on paper.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:30.480
- On any given day, he could
be the world's richest man

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:32.580
or he could be the world's
second richest man,

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:36.660
or he might fall because the
share value of Tesla falls.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.550
- [Narrator] Most of
Musk's wealth is tied up

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:40.320
in shares of his businesses.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:42.780
That means volatility
in his company's stock

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:45.660
and valuations can directly
sway his net worth.

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:47.268
(crowd chatter)
- When I think about Tesla.

00:00:47.268 --> 00:00:48.870
- In the last few months,

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:51.120
Musk has recovered some lost ground.

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:54.630
His net worth, according to
the Bloomberg Billionaire Index

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:57.723
is now estimated at about $160 billion.

00:00:58.560 --> 00:00:59.430
But the trajectory

00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:03.450
of his key businesses has
some investors concerned.

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:05.340
Here's how a volatile stretch for some

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:08.403
of his companies is
impacting Musk's net worth.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:12.810
- Elon Musk's wealth really
ballooned during the pandemic.

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:14.310
But in the past year or so,

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:18.060
we've seen it go on a wild rollercoaster.

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:19.440
- [Narrator] The Wall
Street Journal reached out

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:22.170
to Elon Musk for comment,
but he did not respond.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:25.470
- Since he took over Twitter,
roughly six months ago,

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:26.640
there's been lots of questions

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:30.330
about his overall management
style and wondering if,

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:33.480
perhaps, some of the
magic has been rubbed off.

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:36.180
- [Narrator] Musk is
a serial entrepreneur.

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:40.860
He made $22 million selling
his first startup in 1999,

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:43.350
an internet business called Zip2,

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:46.980
then bet most of that
money on a startup, PayPal.

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:51.510
When eBay bought PayPal,
he made $165 million

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:53.760
and used that to found SpaceX

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:56.610
and become an early investor in Tesla.

00:01:56.610 --> 00:02:00.513
He bought Twitter in October,
2022 for $44 billion,

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:02.790
funding some of the purchase

00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:07.350
by selling $39 billion
worth of his Tesla shares.

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:10.230
It's been a rocky few
months since his takeover.

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:12.570
- Twitter's never been a company
that's made a lot of money,

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:15.630
oftentimes being unprofitable
on an annual basis,

00:02:15.630 --> 00:02:20.630
but he takes control and
immediately he says he needed

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.290
to start making dramatic changes.

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:23.970
- [Narrator] Soon after the purchase,

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:28.290
Musk fired top executives,
laid off thousands of employees

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:30.990
and said advertisers
cutting ad spending have led

00:02:30.990 --> 00:02:33.030
to a massive drop in revenue.

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:36.390
- He thinks he's, in
essence, right size to ship,

00:02:36.390 --> 00:02:37.680
but now it's a private company,

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:40.350
so we don't know exactly
what's going on in there.

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:42.660
- [Narrator] Musk's ambitions
for Twitter are a mix

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:45.240
of content, communication, and commerce,

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:49.050
similar to popular Chinese
social media platform, WeChat.

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:51.960
All this, Musk says,
will help turn Twitter

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:54.633
into a company worth $250 billion.

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:59.040
But for now, Twitter is
valued around $20 billion

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:02.310
- And I remember $20
billion is dramatically less

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:04.107
than what he acquired the company for

00:03:04.107 --> 00:03:07.110
and the deal that was around $44 billion.

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:10.560
So just imagine his wealth going like this

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:12.963
and it's just been a wild ride to watch.

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:17.130
- [Narrator] Elon Musk's main
source of wealth is Tesla.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:21.670
As of late April, 2023, Tesla
was worth about $500 billion

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:25.770
and Musk owns about 13% of the company.

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:28.410
Tesla grew significantly in 2020,

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:32.970
up to a peak value of
$1.2 trillion in 2021.

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:35.400
But it fell significantly last year,

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:38.070
down to around $390 billion.

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:39.420
And all that fluctuation

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:41.970
has affected Musk's personal wealth.

00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:45.630
While Tesla's stock has
rebounded slightly in 2023,

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:47.880
investors have a few concerns.

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:50.610
The amount of time Musk
spends focused on Twitter

00:03:50.610 --> 00:03:53.670
and Tesla's price cuts that
have reduced profit margins

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:55.080
on each car it sells.

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:56.940
- Well, Tesla is profitable,

00:03:56.940 --> 00:04:00.330
and it's projecting a dramatic
growth into the future.

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:04.560
The question is how
dramatic and how profitable.

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:06.270
- [Narrator] Musk also envisions a future

00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:08.910
where Teslas continue
making money for the company

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:11.370
after someone initially purchases the car.

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:14.100
For example, charging
for software updates.

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:15.090
- And that's a big bet.

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:16.410
That's like, in a lot of ways,

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:19.503
an industry upending business model.

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:22.320
Tesla has not yet shown the ability

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:25.950
to deploy fully autonomous
vehicle technology

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:28.267
and so he's essentially telling the world,

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:30.660
"This is coming, and we're
gonna make a lot of money

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:33.723
down the road", and Wall
Street's not so sure about that.

00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:38.190
- [Narrator] And then there's SpaceX.

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:40.650
Musk founded the company in 2002

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:44.100
with money he got from
selling his stake in PayPal.

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:46.740
And while SpaceX doesn't
release financials,

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:50.373
last year the company was
valued at around $140 billion.

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:54.930
As of 2022, a trust
associated with Elon Musk

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:57.510
owned 42% of the company.

00:04:57.510 --> 00:05:00.390
SpaceX executives recently
said it's making money

00:05:00.390 --> 00:05:03.630
off of its Falcon 9 rockets
and Dragon Spacecraft.

00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:07.020
And executives expect
Starlink, a SpaceX division

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:09.060
that provides high
speed broadband internet

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:12.420
with satellites to begin
making money this year too.

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:16.020
- Tesla is where the bulk of
his wealth is at this point,

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:19.560
but SpaceX is increasingly looking like

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:21.780
it's going to be a juggernaut onto its own

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:25.200
and might be where the next tranche

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:28.290
of huge valuation comes from.

00:05:28.290 --> 00:05:30.930
- [Narrator] Musk also
owns three other companies,

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:34.470
Neurolink, Boring Company, and X.AI.

00:05:34.470 --> 00:05:38.880
They're all privately held,
and their finances are unclear.

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:40.890
- They're their early stages.

00:05:40.890 --> 00:05:43.770
The bulk of Elon Musk's time at this point

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:48.510
is in three places, Tesla,
SpaceX, and now Twitter.

00:05:48.510 --> 00:05:51.990
These other startups
are of interest to him,

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:56.220
but he would even say
that they are far down

00:05:56.220 --> 00:05:58.920
on the list of priorities
in any given day.

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:01.230
- [Narrator] Musk's wealth
has traditionally been tied up

00:06:01.230 --> 00:06:03.630
in his businesses and he's been labeled

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:06.900
as a cash poor billionaire
because he has to borrow

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:09.690
against his shares for living expenses.

00:06:09.690 --> 00:06:12.540
- One of the things about
Elon is he's become richer

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:15.990
and richer is that it
gives him the wherewithal

00:06:15.990 --> 00:06:19.650
and the ability to chase
these big ideas that he has.

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:22.350
Whether it's trying to make humanity

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:26.490
a multi-planetary species,
or make electric cars cool,

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:31.440
or buy that shiny object that
he now has, which is Twitter.

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:34.590
A stumble now could change his legacy,

00:06:34.590 --> 00:06:38.460
could perhaps overshadow
his past accomplishments,

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:42.373
yet he's still showing a
huge appetite for risk.

00:06:42.373 --> 00:06:44.956
(bright music)

00:06:46.313 --> 00:06:48.120
(crowd cheer)

